WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.168 --> 00:00:05.046
CATELYN: Family, duty, honor.

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:08.090
Every Tully child learns our words,

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:11.427
but l was a woman before l understood them.

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:13.221
Years before,

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:17.183
my father had taken to foster
the son of a wartime friend,

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.644
a minor lord on the Fingers.

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:23.022
The boy had arrived at our castle
as Petyr Baelish.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.318
Due to his home and size,
my brother soon named him Littlefinger.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:30.029
When l came of age,

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:33.533
Brandon Stark of Winterfell
sought and won my hand.

00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:36.369
To my father, Brandon was heir to the North

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:39.705
and a suitable match
for a daughter of House Tully.

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:41.290
To me,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.129
Brandon was wild and terrifying,
never far from laughter or trouble.

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:51.175
l loved him with all the fire of a first passion,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:55.179
much, l came to realize, as Petyr loved me.

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:59.892
When Petyr heard of my engagement,
he challenged Brandon to a duel.

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:03.771
Petyr survived only because
l begged Brandon not to kill him.

00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:06.816
l still thought of Petyr as family.

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:08.901
Now,

00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:11.320
l wish l had let him die.

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:15.992
Only days before my wedding,
when l thought to be happy forever,

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:20.246
Prince Rhaegar Targaryen abducted
Brandon's sister, Lyanna.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.539
Hot-blooded as always,

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:25.793
Brandon immediately rode for King's Landing
to demand justice,

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:29.338
which the Mad King Aerys Targaryen gave him

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:32.300
in his own twisted fashion.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.429
The day the raven arrived with the news
of my Brandon's death,

00:01:36.722 --> 00:01:40.266
l locked myself in a room
and refused to eat for days

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:43.894
until my father reminded me of my duty.

00:01:44.271 --> 00:01:47.732
l was to marry Eddard,
Brandon's younger brother.

00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:52.361
A man whom l had never met,
though of whom none spoke ill,

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.072
or spoke anything at all.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:02:00.286
Our union would cement an alliance
of the North, Vale,

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:05.499
Stormlands and Riverlands in rebellion
against the Mad King.

00:02:06.043 --> 00:02:07.376
l was a Tully.

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.503
l did my duty.

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:11.505
We were married quickly

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.676
and were spared only one night
before he had to return to the field.

00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:17.511
l spent the war by the windows,

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:22.391
waiting for a raven to hear if my son
would grow up fatherless or at all.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.603
We knew the price of defeat.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:30.816
l scoured the kitchens and washing rooms
for any and all gossip.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:34.111
Robert had won and crushed the Mad King.

00:02:34.196 --> 00:02:37.156
Robert had lost,
but Jaime Lannister was now king.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.116
Robert had almost won,

00:02:39.201 --> 00:02:44.246
but the Mad King had become a dragon
and burned King's Landing to ash.

00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:50.252
At night, l told myself
the war would end soon and bring peace.

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:53.381
Either a victory or the grave.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.009
l was wrong.

00:02:57.678 --> 00:02:58.928
Robert won,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:02.515
and my husband avenged his brother
and my love.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.934
But when he came home to me,

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:08.104
he could not meet my eyes.

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:12.900
l saw the reason by his side.

00:03:13.777 --> 00:03:16.112
Many men have bastards, l know.

00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:17.988
And under the strain of war,

00:03:18.073 --> 00:03:22.535
any man, no matter how honorable,
may forsake his vows for a night of warmth

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:24.453
that he may never know again.

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:28.124
But Ned Stark was not built like other men.

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:32.753
His Northern honor would not let him
sequester his shame

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:35.756
in some distant holdfast.

00:03:35.841 --> 00:03:39.760
He brought this boy, this Jon Snow,

00:03:39.845 --> 00:03:43.139
home to raise with his trueborn children.

00:03:44.307 --> 00:03:45.641
My children.

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:49.311
Yet even these bitter memories are sweet now.

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:52.314
They are all l have left of my Ned.

00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:56.485
Our family is broken and scattered.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.614
And our son must wage a war for the pieces.

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.284
We need to go home.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.244
The Starks are of the North,

00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:09.165
and like the snows of winter,
when they come south,

00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:11.417
they melt away.

